     <period-start iso-date="2023-02-11"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-04-30"></period-end>
     <actual value="0">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam planned at the proposal stage to conduct distribution of winterization assistance (either in cash or kind) to 1,000 households. Initially, the distribution modality was changed to cash during the second weeks of the response, when the overall temperature improved, so as to give beneficiaries the flexibility to purchase items based on their needs. However due to issues related to potential protection risks and data protection risks around cash interventions for earthquake affected areas, Oxfam was not able to implement the activity as planned (Please refer to the final narrative report for more information). Hence, Oxfam requested to change the activity to distribution of Hygiene Kits, to cover the needs of those living in the communities affected by EQ and decrease the risk of a cholera outbreak. The target was also increased accordingly to 5,000 households. As a result the Shelter  whole budget was moved to the WASH sector.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-02-11"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-08-10"></period-end>
     <actual value="0">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam planned at the proposal stage to conduct distribution of winterization assistance (either in cash or kind) to 1,000 households. Initially, the distribution modality was changed to cash during the second weeks of the response, when the overall weather conditions improved, so as to give beneficiaries the flexibility to purchase items based on their needs. However due to the below-mentioned issues (See point 2) related to potential protection risks and data protection risks around cash interventions for earthquake affected areas, Oxfam was not able to implement the activity as planned. Hence, Oxfam requested to change the activity to distribution of Hygiene Kits, to cover the needs of those living in the communities affected by EQ and decrease the risk of a cholera outbreak. The target was also increased accordingly from 2,700 to 5,000 households. As a result the Shelter (SHI)  whole budget was moved to the WASH sector.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
